## Changes Applied

### `tools/` module

| File | Sites | Change |
|---|---|---|
| `consumer/group/ShareGroupCommand.java` | 5 sites | `if (cause instanceof KafkaException) { throw (KafkaException) cause; }` → pattern matching `ke` |
| `consumer/group/ConsumerGroupCommand.java` | 1 site | Same pattern |
| `streams/StreamsGroupCommand.java` | 1 site | Same pattern |
| `streams/TopologyDescriptionFormatter.java` | 3-way chain | `instanceof Source/Processor/Sink` + explicit casts → pattern matching, eliminating 3 separate cast variables |
| `reassign/ReassignPartitionsCommand.java` | 3 sites | `instanceof ActiveMoveState` (2 casts, 1 cast) and `instanceof CancelledMoveState` (2 casts) → pattern matching, eliminating 5 casts total |
| `ConnectPluginPath.java` | 1 site | `instanceof TerseException` + cast → pattern matching |
| `GroupOffsetsResetter.java` | 2 sites | `logEndOffset instanceof LogOffset && offset > ((LogOffset) logEndOffset).value` and same for `logStartOffset` — guarded pattern matching in conjunction condition, eliminating double field access via cast |

### `coordinator-common/` module

| File | Line | Change |
|---|---|---|
| `CoordinatorLoaderImpl.java` | 134 | `logOpt.get()` after `isEmpty()` early-return → `logOpt.orElseThrow()` |

**Reverted:** Three negated-guard `!(x instanceof LogOffset lo)` patterns in `GroupOffsetsResetter` where the guard branch calls `printUsageAndExit` (a `void` method that internally calls `System.exit`). The Java compiler doesn't treat that as a definite termination, so the pattern variable would be considered uninitialized — a compiler error. The positive-guard cases (using `&&` with the field access) were retained since the variable is unambiguously in scope there.

